    source "In 1936, E. W. Dolch identified the 220 most common words encountered in the text children read. This high-frequency word list includes many easily decodable words (e.g., it, get) and some words with irregular parts (e.g., was, said)."
    locator "https://ufli.education.ufl.edu/resources/teaching-resources/instructional-activities/irregular-and-high-frequency-words/"
    trust authoritative

    cites "Pre-Primer (all 40, complete): the, to, and, a, i, you, it, in, said, for, up, look, is, go, we, little, down, can, see, not, one, my, me, big, come, blue, red, where, jump, away, here, help, make, yellow, two, play, run, find, three, funny. Primer (all 52, complete): he, was, that, she, on, they, but, at, with, all, there, out, be, have, am, do, did, what, so, get, like, this, will, yes, went, are, now, no, came, ride, into, good, want, too, pretty, four, saw, well, ran, brown, eat, who, new, must, black, white, soon, our, ate, say, under, please. First Grade (first five of 41): of, his, had, him, her. Second Grade (first five of 46): would, very, your, its, around. Third Grade (all 41, complete): if, long, about, got, six, never, seven, eight, today, myself, much, keep, try, start, ten, bring, drink, only, better, hold, warm, full, done, light, pick, hurt, cut, kind, fall, carry, small, own, show, hot, far, draw, clean, grow, together, shall, laugh. (Transcribed directly from the deck's own level-divider and word-slide text runs, in the deck's true display order resolved via presentation.xml's slide-ID list, not zip filename order.)" locator "https://ufli.education.ufl.edu/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Dolch-Words-Slides.pptx"
}
